Hi folks.

Among other things I'm testing out an additional eu server (in
Ireland) for nao. Ultimately this should share login, save games,
watched games, highscores, everything, with nao.

The two servers in testing now are:

us1.alt.org (eventually nao replacement, Amazon EC2 instance in us-
west-1a)
eu1.alt.org (probable eu.nao, Amazon EC2 instance in eu-west-1a)

I'm looking for folks in europe to help me with testing eu1.

Games started on either are watchable on the other, everything is
shared.

Issues:
* on eu1, the login prompt lags because it is reading the auth file
over the network
* on eu1 loading and saving games is slower than us1. level changes
have a slight latency.
* if a game or game-watcher is on eu1, then the watcher will still be
able to see the game, but it won't be keypress by keypress, but will
jump in intervals. I'm almost positive this is nfs buffering and I can
help this by reducing the window way down for the inprogress games
only. I'll work on this.

But even though certain aspects of eu1 (particularly when just
starting through dgl and initial game load) are currently slow, the
actual gameplay should be _much_ better than nao.

Anyway, looking for feedback. These games should be treated as
throwaway, as nao will eventually sync up and i'll transition us1 to
nao when the time is right. But for now, us1 and eu1 should work
separately from nao as their own connected testbed.

